<!-- ── CLAMSHELL DEEP DIVE ── -->
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow-sub">Clamshell grill-oven</p>
    <h2>The Lang Clamshell — both-sides-simultaneous cooking + hinge-spring service signature</h2>
    <p>The Clamshell is Lang's defining product. Flat cooking surface on the bottom, overhead radiant heating element on the upper platen, the unit closes down on food and cooks from both sides at once. The operational benefit is meaningful: cook times cut 40 to 50 percent on burgers (90 seconds vs 3 minutes), sandwiches, panini, and similar fast-cook items. For LA QSR and fast-casual operations running 200+ covers per day, that throughput difference is operationally consequential — it's the difference between hitting peak-hour service times or falling behind.</p>
    <p>Where Lang Clamshells live in LA: burger concepts, sandwich chains, panini-focused menus, fast-casual operations where speed-to-plate matters. The install base is narrower than general-purpose flat-top griddles (Garland G-series, Imperial ITG) but consistent в the segment that needs the Clamshell specifically.</p>
    <p><strong>Service signature:</strong> the upper platen hinge plus spring tension system is the #1 Clamshell service item. The platen opens and closes hundreds of times per shift — over a year of heavy QSR duty, that's roughly 100,000+ open-close cycles. Hinge bushings wear, springs lose tension, the platen stops closing flush against the lower cooking surface, and the cook pattern becomes uneven. We carry Lang Clamshell hinge kits on the van because we know that's what fails first. Replacement runs $240 to $420 parts-and-labor depending on configuration, completes in 1 to 1.5 hours, and restores even cook pattern immediately.</p>
    <p>Secondary Clamshell service items: lower platen surface re-polishing and re-seasoning at year 4 to 6 ($200 to $340), thermostat calibration drift correction ($200 to $340), heating element replacement (electric variants, $300 to $520), gas valve / SIT control service (gas variants, $260 to $440). Full Clamshell refurbish at year 8 to 10 covering hinge + spring + thermostat + element typically lands $600 to $1,000 — operationally cheaper than replacement.</p>
  </div>
</section>

